1
00:00:55,023 --> 00:00:57,631
(Happy Anding)

2
00:00:58,984 --> 00:01:00,193
(All people, groups, firms, places, and events are fictional.)

3
00:01:00,194 --> 00:01:01,323
(Child actors were filmed safely with their guardians present.)

4
00:01:01,324 --> 00:01:02,553
(Animal scenes were staged under welfare rules.)

5
00:01:02,554 --> 00:01:03,664
(AI-based technology was used in parts of the production.)

6
00:01:06,834 --> 00:01:08,664
Most of my childhood memories consist of...

7
00:01:09,564 --> 00:01:12,004
the clanking of metal, my dad's heavy breathing,

8
00:01:12,904 --> 00:01:17,504
and the laughter from the TV that covered it all up.

9
00:01:19,044 --> 00:01:22,144
For that eccentric kid who loved comedy shows more than toys,

10
00:01:24,244 --> 00:01:27,654
a life-altering incident would occur a few years later.

11
00:01:28,784 --> 00:01:31,024
Rather, it was bound to happen.

12
00:01:34,224 --> 00:01:35,954
Wishing our incoming freshmen...

13
00:01:36,294 --> 00:01:39,824
endless growth and glorious achievements,

14
00:01:40,794 --> 00:01:41,864
I ask you,

15
00:01:42,794 --> 00:01:45,004
as students of the prestigious Hwaseo High,

16
00:01:45,364 --> 00:01:48,004
to uphold our noble spirit and educational philosophy...

17
00:01:48,374 --> 00:01:50,544
and spread them to the world...

18
00:01:50,744 --> 00:01:53,204
- with immense pride and dignity.
- What's with...

19
00:01:53,274 --> 00:01:54,274
I sincerely hope for your commitment.

20
00:01:54,344 --> 00:01:55,374
that pitiful face?

21
00:01:55,444 --> 00:01:58,084
Lastly, I ask you once more to lead the way...

22
00:01:58,384 --> 00:02:00,083
toward an even brighter and prouder future...

23
00:02:00,084 --> 00:02:01,214
- for our prestigious Hwaseo High.
- What's with the tacky fit...

24
00:02:01,284 --> 00:02:02,684
of his pants?

25
00:02:03,184 --> 00:02:04,654
That face is a tough sell.

26
00:02:05,254 --> 00:02:06,584
Thank you.

27
00:02:07,224 --> 00:02:10,564
I'd like to offer my heartfelt congratulations on your admission.

28
00:02:13,224 --> 00:02:16,064
Next, representing the incoming freshmen,

29
00:02:16,334 --> 00:02:18,403
Han Jun Seo from Class 3...

30
00:02:18,404 --> 00:02:21,004
- will read the freshman pledge.
- That's him, right?

31
00:02:21,404 --> 00:02:23,544
The son of the director of Yechan Hospital.

32
00:02:23,804 --> 00:02:25,344
Born with a silver spoon?

33
00:02:25,644 --> 00:02:26,714
Pledge.

34
00:02:27,114 --> 00:02:30,084
As of today, Han Jun Seo and 192 incoming freshmen...

35
00:02:30,484 --> 00:02:32,114
have been admitted to Hwaseo High School.

36
00:02:32,244 --> 00:02:35,384
We'll abide by school regulations, elevate the school's honour,

37
00:02:35,454 --> 00:02:36,884
and, following the spirit of Hwaseo,

38
00:02:37,024 --> 00:02:39,554
in carrying on and developing our school's traditions,

39
00:02:39,654 --> 00:02:41,494
we solemnly pledge...

40
00:02:41,694 --> 00:02:43,024
to take the lead and fulfill our responsibilities.

41
00:02:43,524 --> 00:02:44,764
March 3, 2008...

42
00:02:45,364 --> 00:02:47,464
Freshman representative, Han Jun Seo.

43
00:02:50,864 --> 00:02:54,034
Seriously, he's funnier than most comedians.

44
00:02:54,104 --> 00:02:56,174
- Totally.
- You're exaggerating.

45
00:02:57,044 --> 00:02:59,404
- I'm telling you, he's insane.
- Hey, do it one more time.

46
00:02:59,474 --> 00:03:00,874
What, do you think I just do whatever you ask,

47
00:03:00,944 --> 00:03:02,144
just like this?

48
00:03:02,974 --> 00:03:04,244
That's Kim Nam Il from Class 5, right?

49
00:03:04,384 --> 00:03:07,214
- I heard he's a total nutjob.
- He's hilarious, though.

50
00:03:10,084 --> 00:03:11,124
The absolute best.

51
00:03:11,524 --> 00:03:13,554
- I don't like him much.
- Not funny at all.

52
00:03:15,524 --> 00:03:17,724
That's not how you deliver it.

53
00:03:18,394 --> 00:03:19,624
Now, this is what I'm talking about.

54
00:03:23,134 --> 00:03:24,134
Wrong.

55
00:03:24,704 --> 00:03:26,264
Hey, it goes like this.

56
00:03:26,904 --> 00:03:28,134
Now, this is what I'm talking about.

57
00:03:28,874 --> 00:03:29,904
Wrong.

58
00:03:30,374 --> 00:03:31,874
Now, this is what I'm talking about.

59
00:03:32,974 --> 00:03:34,644
Now, this is what I'm talking about.

60
00:03:34,714 --> 00:03:35,714
Now, this is what I'm talking about.

61
00:03:35,774 --> 00:03:38,644
- Good morning.
- All right, page 44.

62
00:03:40,554 --> 00:03:41,854
Those seats are empty. What's going on?

63
00:03:48,094 --> 00:03:49,654
Now, this is what I'm talking about.

64
00:03:49,754 --> 00:03:50,824
Now, this is what I'm talking about.

65
00:03:50,894 --> 00:03:52,064
Now, this is what I'm talking about.

66
00:03:56,764 --> 00:03:58,404
Wrap it up and get out here.

67
00:04:01,374 --> 00:04:02,374
Holy crap.

68
00:04:05,544 --> 00:04:06,914
Hey, I just saw a snake.

69
00:04:07,544 --> 00:04:09,614
Geez, quit being dramatic and just do it.

70
00:04:12,544 --> 00:04:15,954
Freshman class rep. What are you doing?

71
00:04:16,084 --> 00:04:18,654
See, this is why you really can't judge a book by its cover.

72
00:04:19,284 --> 00:04:21,494
Hey, your dad was on TV and said, you know,

73
00:04:21,694 --> 00:04:23,664
that smoking puts holes in your bones.

74
00:04:23,724 --> 00:04:25,064
So what do you think you're doing?

75
00:04:25,394 --> 00:04:27,064
His dad is on TV? Is he an actor?

76
00:04:27,834 --> 00:04:28,834
You seriously don't know?

77
00:04:28,894 --> 00:04:30,634
You know that show every Sunday morning,

78
00:04:30,804 --> 00:04:32,064
something like "Era of Great Doctors"?

79
00:04:32,304 --> 00:04:34,404
The famous doctor on it is his dad.

80
00:04:34,604 --> 00:04:37,544
Your grandfather is a doctor, your dad is a doctor,

81
00:04:37,674 --> 00:04:40,103
and your brother goes to Hankuk Med, right?

82
00:04:40,104 --> 00:04:41,173
What does it matter if he is?

83
00:04:41,174 --> 00:04:42,774
Why do you care so much about other people's business?

84
00:04:42,844 --> 00:04:44,844
I don't care. Everyone else does.

85
00:04:48,014 --> 00:04:49,854
What are you doing? Come out so we can clean.

86
00:04:55,094 --> 00:04:58,064
Hey, you really should quit smoking.

87
00:04:58,324 --> 00:05:00,634
How heartbroken would your dad be if he found out?

88
00:05:07,304 --> 00:05:08,304
What?

89
00:05:09,804 --> 00:05:10,804
What do you want?

90
00:05:14,874 --> 00:05:16,344
Your parents must be even more heartbroken.

91
00:05:19,344 --> 00:05:20,384
What did you just say?

92
00:05:22,214 --> 00:05:23,254
You little punk.

93
00:05:24,154 --> 00:05:25,254
Take it outside.

94
00:05:28,794 --> 00:05:30,424
- You piece of...
- You bastard.

95
00:05:30,524 --> 00:05:33,934
- I told you to take it outside.
- Hey...

96
00:05:33,994 --> 00:05:35,194
I got crap on my hands.

97
00:05:36,594 --> 00:05:40,274
- You jerk.
- Freeze!

98
00:05:44,904 --> 00:05:45,944
You crazy bastard.

99
00:05:46,804 --> 00:05:48,014
Sir, his knees are touching the floor.

100
00:05:48,074 --> 00:05:49,614
No, they're not. Not at all, sir.

101
00:05:49,914 --> 00:05:51,014
- Hold that position properly.
- Yes, sir.

102
00:05:51,844 --> 00:05:54,513
Starting today, until graduation, you three are on bathroom duty.

103
00:05:54,514 --> 00:05:55,514
Got it?

104
00:05:55,515 --> 00:05:57,084
- What?
- Sir.

105
00:05:57,324 --> 00:05:59,284
That seems a bit unfair, sir.

106
00:05:59,754 --> 00:06:00,824
Excuse me, Mr. Jung.

107
00:06:01,494 --> 00:06:02,494
Yes?

108
00:06:10,194 --> 00:06:11,634
Here are the sign-ups for the broadcasting festival.

109
00:06:12,464 --> 00:06:15,074
Did a lot of people sign up?

110
00:06:15,174 --> 00:06:16,234
- What's his deal?
- No.

111
00:06:16,304 --> 00:06:17,603
- Why is he looking like that?
- What should we do?

112
00:06:17,604 --> 00:06:19,474
The vice principal said that if we're short again this year,

113
00:06:19,604 --> 00:06:21,774
he'll cancel the festival.

114
00:06:26,584 --> 00:06:27,614
Get up, you three.

115
00:06:33,924 --> 00:06:35,424
You perform at the broadcasting festival.

116
00:06:35,554 --> 00:06:37,164
Then I'll let you off bathroom duty.

117
00:06:37,424 --> 00:06:38,424
What?

118
00:06:38,724 --> 00:06:41,394
- I don't want to embarrass myself.
- I'll just clean.

119
00:06:43,634 --> 00:06:44,634
We'll do it.

120
00:06:47,874 --> 00:06:48,874
We'll perform.

121
00:06:49,504 --> 00:06:50,544
We'll do it, sir.

122
00:06:53,814 --> 00:06:55,174
Don't worry about a thing.

123
00:07:07,594 --> 00:07:09,194
I mean, I went ahead and agreed,

124
00:07:09,294 --> 00:07:10,724
but what are the three of us supposed to do?

125
00:07:11,494 --> 00:07:13,124
Hey, can you dance?

126
00:07:13,424 --> 00:07:15,164
- No.
- Can you sing?

127
00:07:15,334 --> 00:07:17,834
- I'm terrible.
- What are you even good at?

128
00:07:18,434 --> 00:07:19,864
- Studying.
- Darn it.

129
00:07:24,344 --> 00:07:25,374
Let's do comedy.

130
00:07:26,244 --> 00:07:27,244
Comedy?

131
00:07:27,614 --> 00:07:28,974
If we just take how our teachers act...

132
00:07:29,044 --> 00:07:30,884
and do quick impressions, the kids will love it.

133
00:07:33,284 --> 00:07:34,454
That doesn't sound bad.

134
00:07:34,984 --> 00:07:35,984
Whatever.

135
00:07:36,414 --> 00:07:38,484
All right. It's settled then.

136
00:07:39,154 --> 00:07:41,524
Okay, push all the desks back.

137
00:07:46,194 --> 00:07:50,764
(The 12th Broadcasting Festival: Moonlight Paradise)

138
00:07:50,934 --> 00:07:53,064
(Green Room)

139
00:07:56,674 --> 00:07:58,643
That was an amazing performance.

140
00:07:58,644 --> 00:08:00,573
- Let's give them a big hand again.
- Aren't you nervous?

141
00:08:00,574 --> 00:08:02,774
No, I've been on stages much bigger than this.

142
00:08:03,744 --> 00:08:05,444
When I won the Math Olympiad award,

143
00:08:05,544 --> 00:08:07,354
that stage was about three times this size.

144
00:08:07,414 --> 00:08:09,014
Right, good for you.

145
00:08:09,284 --> 00:08:10,424
Three times bigger, my foot.

146
00:08:10,484 --> 00:08:12,554
Now that we know him, he's the biggest nutjob.

147
00:08:12,624 --> 00:08:13,654
Thanks.

148
00:08:14,124 --> 00:08:15,293
Next up is a comedy sketch...

149
00:08:15,294 --> 00:08:16,623
prepared by Kang Tae Gu from Class 2,

150
00:08:16,624 --> 00:08:20,464
Kim Nam Il from Class 5, and Han Jun Seo from Class 3.

151
00:08:21,534 --> 00:08:22,764
Hey, wait...

152
00:08:25,704 --> 00:08:26,904
Come on, that's so childish.

153
00:08:28,304 --> 00:08:29,334
Hey, hurry up, let's go.

154
00:08:31,274 --> 00:08:35,474
One, two, three. Let's go.

155
00:08:35,674 --> 00:08:39,744
- Nam Il...
- Hey, wait...

156
00:08:41,254 --> 00:08:42,684
Lastly...

157
00:08:46,454 --> 00:08:49,054
- Don't say "lastly".
- Lastly...

158
00:08:50,464 --> 00:08:53,624
Freeze!

159
00:09:00,204 --> 00:09:01,204
Lastly...

160
00:09:12,744 --> 00:09:14,054
It was a crude performance.

161
00:09:17,454 --> 00:09:19,884
The makeup, the acting...

162
00:09:21,994 --> 00:09:23,124
Everything was a mess.

163
00:09:24,894 --> 00:09:26,364
On an old, creaky,

164
00:09:27,164 --> 00:09:29,094
tiny 33m² stage.

165
00:09:52,954 --> 00:09:55,824
(The 12th Broadcasting Festival: Moonlight Paradise)

166
00:10:07,704 --> 00:10:10,844
I felt something.

167
00:10:15,274 --> 00:10:17,213
Let's hear it for these three friends...

168
00:10:17,214 --> 00:10:18,613
who brought us so much laughter.

169
00:10:18,614 --> 00:10:21,554
Let's give them another big round of applause, please.

170
00:11:31,084 --> 00:11:32,084
They laughed.

171
00:11:36,194 --> 00:11:37,194
The kids...

172
00:11:39,364 --> 00:11:42,064
They were laughing at us.

173
00:12:11,094 --> 00:12:13,224
They laughed. They laughed at us.

174
00:12:14,134 --> 00:12:16,734
(Audition Ticket: Kang Tae Gu)

175
00:12:16,794 --> 00:12:19,534
(Audition Ticket: Kim Nam Il)

176
00:12:19,604 --> 00:12:22,274
(Audition Ticket: Han Jun Seo)

177
00:12:33,544 --> 00:12:37,724
(Long Live Comedy)

178
00:12:45,364 --> 00:12:50,334
(Episode 1: Ten Years Already)

179
00:12:50,394 --> 00:12:51,404
How full is it?

180
00:12:51,604 --> 00:12:53,504
I don't know. It's too dark to tell.

181
00:12:54,404 --> 00:12:57,234
I'm not even asking for a full house, just half.

182
00:13:00,504 --> 00:13:02,114
Whatever you imagine,

183
00:13:02,444 --> 00:13:04,214
you'll see so much more.

184
00:13:04,814 --> 00:13:07,684
Introducing Korea's top comedy trio.

185
00:13:08,454 --> 00:13:09,484
A.

186
00:13:10,084 --> 00:13:11,384
Su.

187
00:13:12,354 --> 00:13:15,324
Ra!

188
00:13:18,864 --> 00:13:20,834
- Hello. We're here...
- To turn your minds...

189
00:13:20,894 --> 00:13:21,894
into total chaos.

190
00:13:22,094 --> 00:13:23,464
- We're Asura!
- We're Asura!

191
00:13:29,504 --> 00:13:32,544
Turn off the lights. I can't sleep...

192
00:13:45,084 --> 00:13:47,353
If you're drunk, you should go home.

193
00:13:47,354 --> 00:13:49,694
If you hit it off, get a room.

194
00:13:49,794 --> 00:13:53,294
Why come to someone else's theater and make out like that?

195
00:13:53,394 --> 00:13:55,093
Stop talking and work on the ending.

196
00:13:55,094 --> 00:13:56,194
Don't we have a sketch review tomorrow?

197
00:13:56,864 --> 00:13:58,404
I already worked it out.

198
00:13:59,804 --> 00:14:02,434
- Watch this. I told you...
- You always jump straight...

199
00:14:02,504 --> 00:14:03,674
into dancing, with no brain at all.

200
00:14:03,874 --> 00:14:05,344
You care about getting gigs more than being funny.

201
00:14:05,404 --> 00:14:06,504
Think I don't know?

202
00:14:06,574 --> 00:14:08,513
- Don't you want to make money?
- Oh, give me a break.

203
00:14:08,514 --> 00:14:10,114
That's why you'll never make it, man.

204
00:14:10,214 --> 00:14:12,284
If I don't make it, neither do you, you idiot.

205
00:14:12,344 --> 00:14:14,414
You've got a point there, man. I'll try harder, man.

206
00:14:14,484 --> 00:14:16,654
- Hey, what are you writing?
- You never know.

207
00:14:17,014 --> 00:14:18,084
Just jotting it all down.

208
00:14:18,154 --> 00:14:20,324
You psycho. Give it here.

209
00:14:20,384 --> 00:14:22,454
- Let go. Hey.
- Hey, let go of my hand.

210
00:14:22,824 --> 00:14:25,794
Hey, how about this? That couple just gave me an idea...

211
00:14:26,294 --> 00:14:28,434
- Slapstick.
- About time for some slapstick.

212
00:14:28,694 --> 00:14:30,964
It's the Joseon era, a noble newlywed couple.

213
00:14:31,104 --> 00:14:32,104
Good setup.

214
00:14:32,204 --> 00:14:34,503
On their wedding night, the bride gets shy,

215
00:14:34,504 --> 00:14:35,734
so he tries to blow out the candle, but it won't go out.

216
00:14:36,034 --> 00:14:38,043
- Then what?
- He has to blow it out somehow.

217
00:14:38,044 --> 00:14:40,673
Right. But then the bride loses her patience,

218
00:14:40,674 --> 00:14:42,514
shoves the groom aside, and then...

219
00:14:46,984 --> 00:14:48,884
Lifts her skirt like this.

220
00:14:57,864 --> 00:14:59,224
- Trash it.
- Trash it.

221
00:15:00,864 --> 00:15:03,364
- Why? I think it's funny.
- Your sense of humour sucks.

222
00:15:03,494 --> 00:15:06,434
Jun Seo, name just one skit you pushed that actually did well.

223
00:15:14,274 --> 00:15:16,614
- She glared at us again.
- Why is she glaring?

224
00:15:16,674 --> 00:15:19,813
- It's almost closing time.
- Well, she could just come tell us.

225
00:15:19,814 --> 00:15:21,283
Why does she always give us dirty looks?

226
00:15:21,284 --> 00:15:23,554
Jun Seo, you go this way. Hey, let's head this way.

227
00:15:24,354 --> 00:15:25,384
The ice...

228
00:15:26,824 --> 00:15:29,094
Walking on eggshells around my boss by day,

229
00:15:29,394 --> 00:15:31,224
and around a cafe barista by night.

230
00:15:32,064 --> 00:15:34,164
How did my life end up like this?

231
00:15:34,734 --> 00:15:37,604
Hey, listen. What if three obnoxious customers...

232
00:15:37,734 --> 00:15:39,934
Knock it off already. Let's just take a break.

233
00:15:40,034 --> 00:15:41,434
We'll be writing more at home anyway.

234
00:15:41,904 --> 00:15:43,603
Why are you complaining before you even hear it?

235
00:15:43,604 --> 00:15:44,974
What if it's not about comedy?

236
00:15:46,044 --> 00:15:47,044
It's not?

237
00:15:49,814 --> 00:15:50,884
How did you know?

238
00:15:51,484 --> 00:15:53,944
I really can't stand him.

239
00:15:54,014 --> 00:15:56,084
I hate him more than that barista back there.

240
00:15:57,724 --> 00:15:58,784
Still, she's kind of cute.

241
00:16:01,809 --> 00:16:02,909
Smells good.

242
00:16:03,979 --> 00:16:05,049
Looks delicious.

243
00:16:05,909 --> 00:16:07,619
(Asura)

244
00:16:07,779 --> 00:16:10,119
You're doing it wrong, man. Give it here.

245
00:16:10,379 --> 00:16:11,519
Let me show you.

246
00:16:11,849 --> 00:16:15,319
Grab it tight right here, okay? Stretch it out, then pull back.

247
00:16:15,459 --> 00:16:16,589
Hey, look right here.

248
00:16:17,389 --> 00:16:19,428
Look at my lats popping. See that?

249
00:16:19,429 --> 00:16:20,799
Hey, wait, what are you wearing?

250
00:16:21,459 --> 00:16:23,398
What do you mean? It's my lats. Check it out.

251
00:16:23,399 --> 00:16:25,029
What's this? Aren't these my boxers?

252
00:16:26,229 --> 00:16:27,239
Take them off.

253
00:16:27,299 --> 00:16:28,438
There's no "yours" or "mine" in this house.

254
00:16:28,439 --> 00:16:29,439
Don't you wear mine?

255
00:16:29,440 --> 00:16:31,309
Those match Na Yeon's, you lunatic. Take them off.

256
00:16:31,509 --> 00:16:32,969
- Chill.
- Take them off, you punk.

257
00:16:33,039 --> 00:16:34,239
I've known her for years, too.

258
00:16:34,339 --> 00:16:35,409
I said take them off. Go take them off.

259
00:16:35,479 --> 00:16:36,609
We're close enough for this, aren't we?

260
00:16:36,679 --> 00:16:38,009
Hey, you punk, I'm going to smash your head in.

261
00:16:38,079 --> 00:16:39,449
Hey. Take them off. Take them off right now.

262
00:16:39,509 --> 00:16:40,578
Then go bring me another pair, jerk.

263
00:16:40,579 --> 00:16:43,018
- Take them off, seriously.
- No way, they're so pretty.

264
00:16:43,019 --> 00:16:44,019
Time to eat.

265
00:16:44,549 --> 00:16:45,619
Take them off after you eat.

266
00:16:45,689 --> 00:16:47,359
I might actually smash your head in.

267
00:16:47,419 --> 00:16:48,458
Why be so stingy?

268
00:16:48,459 --> 00:16:49,789
Yes, chicken skewers.

269
00:16:49,859 --> 00:16:50,859
Looks good.

270
00:16:52,129 --> 00:16:54,729
The last customers last night were wasted and left all of this behind.

271
00:16:55,699 --> 00:16:56,699
Lucky us.

272
00:16:57,499 --> 00:16:58,598
Wait, so this is...

273
00:16:58,599 --> 00:17:01,339
Food-poisoning salmonella is vulnerable to heat,

274
00:17:01,469 --> 00:17:04,268
so heating it above 75 degrees for over a minute kills it all.

275
00:17:04,269 --> 00:17:05,309
It won't kill you.

276
00:17:05,569 --> 00:17:07,069
- It won't?
- Nope.

277
00:17:07,139 --> 00:17:08,139
- Hey, Jun Seo.
- What?

278
00:17:09,209 --> 00:17:11,208
Saving money is great, but come on...

279
00:17:11,209 --> 00:17:12,948
Last month's maintenance fee was 78 dollars,

280
00:17:12,949 --> 00:17:14,619
and the gas was 84 dollars.

281
00:17:14,679 --> 00:17:15,679
Compared to last month, that's...

282
00:17:15,749 --> 00:17:16,979
- It's delicious.
- Thanks for the food.

283
00:17:17,049 --> 00:17:19,288
- It tastes good anyway.
- While we're on the subject,

284
00:17:19,289 --> 00:17:21,119
I think we're going through daily essentials way too fast.

285
00:17:21,189 --> 00:17:22,719
The toilet paper in the bathroom is completely gone.

286
00:17:22,819 --> 00:17:25,029
I told you, right? Just two wraps each time.

287
00:17:26,359 --> 00:17:28,459
This is three wraps. This is two.

288
00:17:29,499 --> 00:17:31,969
The paper dissolves way too fast for that.

289
00:17:32,269 --> 00:17:33,828
Hey, I'm not asking for three-ply.

290
00:17:33,829 --> 00:17:35,669
Can't we just buy something a little thicker?

291
00:17:37,169 --> 00:17:38,169
I'll consider it.

292
00:17:38,239 --> 00:17:40,068
- Thank you, Your Highness.
- Thank you so much.

293
00:17:40,069 --> 00:17:41,539
(Make Frugality a Habit)

294
00:17:41,609 --> 00:17:42,878
That was a big decision.

295
00:17:42,879 --> 00:17:44,979
When did they put that up?

296
00:17:45,409 --> 00:17:46,409
Should I take it down?

297
00:17:47,419 --> 00:17:48,679
No, leave it.

298
00:17:49,219 --> 00:17:50,579
Never helpful in life, honestly...

299
00:17:51,249 --> 00:17:53,049
And on top of that, they put it up crooked.

300
00:17:54,519 --> 00:17:55,558
By the way...

301
00:17:55,559 --> 00:17:58,059
Why don't those guys do YouTube like the other comedians?

302
00:17:58,129 --> 00:18:00,529
They do. It's just nobody watches.

303
00:18:00,699 --> 00:18:03,059
Because they only post clips of their stage performances.

304
00:18:03,429 --> 00:18:05,499
Or videos of themselves rehearsing backstage.

305
00:18:05,699 --> 00:18:06,899
Who watches that kind of stuff?

306
00:18:08,099 --> 00:18:11,239
They could do pranks or alter egos.

307
00:18:13,409 --> 00:18:15,909
Leave them be. They say they love the stage.

308
00:18:16,409 --> 00:18:17,909
Live on the stage,

309
00:18:18,479 --> 00:18:20,009
die on the stage.

310
00:18:21,619 --> 00:18:23,419
They've got to live the way they want.

311
00:18:23,549 --> 00:18:24,549
Still...

312
00:18:25,549 --> 00:18:27,219
Those boys just don't have that killer instinct.

313
00:18:27,489 --> 00:18:28,819
They're fools, absolute fools.

314
00:18:30,519 --> 00:18:32,758
I hope today's sketch review goes well.

315
00:18:32,759 --> 00:18:34,929
I wonder how they're doing.

316
00:18:37,469 --> 00:18:39,399
- Hurry up and come out.
- Hey.

317
00:18:39,729 --> 00:18:40,869
What's this?

318
00:18:42,899 --> 00:18:44,169
- What?
- What's that?

319
00:18:46,339 --> 00:18:49,539
Hey, this is really expensive. Nice.

320
00:18:49,609 --> 00:18:51,379
- What's this?
- Thanks for the treat.

321
00:18:51,449 --> 00:18:52,809
Hey, why are you drinking that?

322
00:18:52,909 --> 00:18:54,449
What if it was delivered to the wrong place?

323
00:18:54,919 --> 00:18:57,949
Why? Maybe someone left it for us to drink.

324
00:18:58,149 --> 00:18:59,219
Like who?

325
00:19:02,589 --> 00:19:04,089
Our fans?

326
00:19:13,099 --> 00:19:15,039
Hey, look at you. Feeling good today?

327
00:19:15,099 --> 00:19:17,269
- You're on a roll today.
- He's feeling good.

328
00:19:18,009 --> 00:19:19,909
I'm drinking it. It'll spoil if we leave it here.

329
00:19:22,039 --> 00:19:25,309
- It hits right away. Good stuff.
- Good?

330
00:19:34,859 --> 00:19:39,229
As expected, you can't beat natural talent.

331
00:19:39,289 --> 00:19:41,259
- So reliable. Truly.
- Unbeatable.

332
00:19:44,399 --> 00:19:46,269
What's wrong? Stomachache?

333
00:19:46,329 --> 00:19:47,998
I don't know. Maybe that drink was bad.

334
00:19:47,999 --> 00:19:50,139
Serves you right for gulping it down like an idiot.

335
00:19:50,199 --> 00:19:51,739
It might just be nerves.

336
00:19:54,579 --> 00:19:56,108
- Here, a calming pill.
- Oh, thanks.

337
00:19:56,109 --> 00:19:57,508
- Hey.
- Thanks... What?

338
00:19:57,509 --> 00:20:00,819
Take only half. Don't space out after taking the whole thing again.

339
00:20:01,749 --> 00:20:02,919
Man, I need to use the restroom again.

340
00:20:02,979 --> 00:20:04,018
- Hey, gather around.
- What?

341
00:20:04,019 --> 00:20:05,289
Gather around, come on.

342
00:20:08,689 --> 00:20:10,859
You know the drill, right? If you chicken out, you lose.

343
00:20:11,029 --> 00:20:13,158
- Don't let the crew scare you.
- Okay...

344
00:20:13,159 --> 00:20:15,498
- Focus your eyes and bring energy.
- Okay...

345
00:20:15,499 --> 00:20:16,899
- Got it?
- Got it.

346
00:20:16,959 --> 00:20:19,329
- All right.
- Hurry up. Quick. Let's go.

347
00:20:19,599 --> 00:20:21,269
- Asura!
- We can do this!

348
00:20:21,339 --> 00:20:22,739
Go, go, go!

349
00:20:22,799 --> 00:20:24,739
- Come out quickly. We're late.
- I'll be right there.

350
00:20:25,709 --> 00:20:29,509
Darn it... They said it would hit the daily limit today.

351
00:20:31,949 --> 00:20:34,819
- Next team.
- Next team, please come in.

352
00:20:35,949 --> 00:20:37,589
- Hello.
- Hello.

353
00:20:37,649 --> 00:20:39,389
- Hello.
- Hello.

354
00:20:41,319 --> 00:20:43,819
Producer Park, how have you been this past week?

355
00:20:44,489 --> 00:20:45,758
Cut the crap.

356
00:20:45,759 --> 00:20:47,029
You come here weekly, so why the formality?

357
00:20:48,399 --> 00:20:50,999
Well, your well-being is the well-being of Gag Jirak.

358
00:20:51,199 --> 00:20:53,569
I always wonder if you've eaten well,

359
00:20:53,629 --> 00:20:55,169
slept well,

360
00:20:55,369 --> 00:20:56,738
or how the stocks you recently bought are doing...

361
00:20:56,739 --> 00:20:57,769
Come on...

362
00:21:00,569 --> 00:21:03,539
Enough. Stop fooling around and just start.

363
00:21:04,609 --> 00:21:05,609
Yes, sir.

364
00:21:09,749 --> 00:21:11,049
Everyone, I'm here today...

365
00:21:11,119 --> 00:21:12,849
because I heard about a primitive tribe...

366
00:21:12,919 --> 00:21:15,559
that has never been touched by modern civilization.

367
00:21:15,889 --> 00:21:20,429
So they don't feel alienated, I dressed up like a caveman.

368
00:21:20,629 --> 00:21:21,998
Do I look like one?

369
00:21:21,999 --> 00:21:23,199
(Put away the chairs after the rehearsal.)

370
00:21:27,299 --> 00:21:30,139
Yes? Perfect, you say? All right, then without further ado,

371
00:21:30,199 --> 00:21:32,309
let's go meet them.

372
00:21:33,509 --> 00:21:34,609
As we speak,

373
00:21:34,679 --> 00:21:36,339
it seems like they're making their appearance.

374
00:21:42,119 --> 00:21:43,549
They look remarkably sharp, don't they?

375
00:21:51,059 --> 00:21:52,359
Are they laughing at me?

376
00:22:17,079 --> 00:22:19,249
That concludes the new sketch reviews.

377
00:22:26,429 --> 00:22:28,059
Shoot...

378
00:22:28,299 --> 00:22:29,659
It dropped again. Seriously.

379
00:22:32,169 --> 00:22:34,269
What are you doing? Get out.

380
00:22:39,639 --> 00:22:40,639
Excuse me, sir.

381
00:22:40,769 --> 00:22:42,979
We haven't received any feedback for weeks.

382
00:22:43,109 --> 00:22:44,409
If you don't like the ending,

383
00:22:44,479 --> 00:22:46,579
- we have other versions...
- It's just bad.

384
00:22:46,709 --> 00:22:47,879
It's not funny.

385
00:22:53,589 --> 00:22:55,889
You should at least tell us why,

386
00:22:55,959 --> 00:22:57,259
- so we can revise...
- Hey.

387
00:22:58,959 --> 00:23:00,089
Are you lecturing me right now?

388
00:23:01,059 --> 00:23:02,299
No, that's not what I meant.

389
00:23:11,339 --> 00:23:14,309
Hey. Why have you been so hard to reach?

390
00:23:14,379 --> 00:23:15,439
Are you freezing me out?

391
00:23:15,609 --> 00:23:17,949
I heard you play golf with Producer Jang all the time.

392
00:23:18,009 --> 00:23:19,209
I know everything, okay?

393
00:23:19,549 --> 00:23:20,609
Tonight?

394
00:23:21,849 --> 00:23:24,279
I have a team dinner tonight. How about tomorrow?

395
00:23:27,089 --> 00:23:28,319
I know, right?

396
00:23:29,489 --> 00:23:31,429
I told you, I found a great place.

397
00:23:32,159 --> 00:23:33,159
Yes.

398
00:23:34,159 --> 00:23:35,599
You son of a...

399
00:23:37,099 --> 00:23:38,169
He didn't even watch it.

400
00:23:39,569 --> 00:23:40,629
My goodness.

401
00:23:41,899 --> 00:23:45,139
- Long time no see.
- What's the occasion today?

402
00:23:45,709 --> 00:23:47,709
If it isn't superstar Hwang.

403
00:23:47,779 --> 00:23:49,739
My debut classmate, Hwang Chan Sung.

404
00:23:54,309 --> 00:23:56,379
Tae Gu. Long time no see.

405
00:23:56,619 --> 00:23:59,719
Why didn't you come to the reunion? Everyone wanted to see you.

406
00:24:00,389 --> 00:24:02,189
I was busy working my part-time job.

407
00:24:04,359 --> 00:24:06,459
Deliveries? Hey, isn't it...

408
00:24:06,529 --> 00:24:09,299
- tough on you?
- I'm fine.

409
00:24:10,059 --> 00:24:11,069
It's kind of fun, actually.

410
00:24:11,129 --> 00:24:12,899
A comedian should be on television.

411
00:24:13,529 --> 00:24:15,499
How did your new sketch go?

412
00:24:17,869 --> 00:24:19,369
I think we have to start from scratch.

413
00:24:19,439 --> 00:24:20,809
- Did it get rejected?
- Yes...

414
00:24:21,879 --> 00:24:24,009
Rejected again? Darn it.

415
00:24:24,279 --> 00:24:26,279
It's been over a year since you passed one, right?

416
00:24:27,919 --> 00:24:30,519
I mean, with you guys trying this hard,

417
00:24:30,719 --> 00:24:33,489
he could at least let you tape one. What more does he want from you?

418
00:24:33,989 --> 00:24:36,889
Bbakgu is really crossing the line, darn it.

419
00:24:41,829 --> 00:24:44,329
Should I put in a good word for you?

420
00:24:46,199 --> 00:24:47,229
Why would you?

421
00:24:49,639 --> 00:24:52,539
Don't tell me this is about you...

422
00:24:52,609 --> 00:24:54,169
ripping off my sketch back then?

423
00:24:54,779 --> 00:24:57,749
Hey, forget it. That was ages ago.

424
00:24:57,849 --> 00:24:59,449
It's fine, man. Just forget about it.

425
00:25:00,109 --> 00:25:02,319
Hey, I told you before,

426
00:25:02,379 --> 00:25:03,649
I was just watching TV by chance and...

427
00:25:03,719 --> 00:25:06,149
Well, some people...

428
00:25:06,219 --> 00:25:09,789
seem to talk behind your back, saying you only became a comedian...

429
00:25:09,859 --> 00:25:10,888
because you stole my sketch.

430
00:25:10,889 --> 00:25:13,329
Hey, does that even make sense?

431
00:25:13,459 --> 00:25:14,829
Success comes to those who are destined for it.

432
00:25:14,899 --> 00:25:16,199
Right?

433
00:25:19,399 --> 00:25:21,569
Hey, Hwang Chan Sung.

434
00:25:21,769 --> 00:25:23,439
You know we have the team dinner tonight, right?

435
00:25:23,499 --> 00:25:25,408
Make sure you come. We can't do it without the star.

436
00:25:25,409 --> 00:25:26,469
Of course, Producer Park.

437
00:25:26,539 --> 00:25:28,439
- I'll be there.
- Be there, be there.

438
00:25:36,379 --> 00:25:37,649
- See you soon.
- Yes, sir.

439
00:25:42,489 --> 00:25:45,729
Hey, I'd love to chat more,

440
00:25:46,189 --> 00:25:47,359
but I have to go, okay?

441
00:25:47,899 --> 00:25:50,229
You guys should come along and...

442
00:25:52,799 --> 00:25:53,869
Never mind.

443
00:25:54,099 --> 00:25:57,169
It might be a little awkward without a sketch on the air. Right?

444
00:25:57,569 --> 00:25:58,909
Take care, okay?

445
00:25:58,969 --> 00:26:00,109
See you around.

446
00:26:00,869 --> 00:26:01,979
See you.

447
00:26:05,979 --> 00:26:07,549
Not like he'd actually help.

448
00:26:10,679 --> 00:26:11,749
Hey.

449
00:26:12,889 --> 00:26:13,919
Let's go, too.

450
00:26:14,789 --> 00:26:15,789
To the team dinner.

451
00:26:18,329 --> 00:26:19,329
Hey.

452
00:26:20,729 --> 00:26:22,099
Just trust me and follow my lead.

453
00:26:23,499 --> 00:26:25,299
I'm going to butter him up properly.

454
00:26:28,069 --> 00:26:29,839
- Darn it.
- Thank you.

455
00:26:31,069 --> 00:26:34,009
- Hello.
- Hello.

456
00:26:35,639 --> 00:26:37,439
The standards keep dropping for that.

457
00:26:37,509 --> 00:26:39,848
- No, not at all.
- He, back then,

458
00:26:39,849 --> 00:26:41,149
He was good.

459
00:26:41,319 --> 00:26:42,419
he used to do this.

460
00:26:45,189 --> 00:26:46,488
Hey, what are you saying?

461
00:26:46,489 --> 00:26:47,519
Let's go over there.

462
00:26:50,119 --> 00:26:51,659
Yes, hey, hello.

463
00:26:56,099 --> 00:26:57,599
- Excuse me, Tae Gu.
- Yes?

464
00:26:57,659 --> 00:26:59,669
This table is for the Quick Service team.

465
00:27:00,129 --> 00:27:01,129
Then we'll go over here.

466
00:27:01,199 --> 00:27:04,039
That's for the Rimimiki seniors...

467
00:27:04,199 --> 00:27:07,609
- Then over there...
- That's Home Ground's table...

468
00:27:07,669 --> 00:27:10,879
Then where are we supposed to sit, you punk?

469
00:27:13,609 --> 00:27:14,819
Oh, boy.

470
00:27:21,489 --> 00:27:23,989
Even if we don't have a sketch, isn't this a bit much?

471
00:27:24,059 --> 00:27:26,329
My stomach hurts. Why do I still feel so bloated?

472
00:27:26,389 --> 00:27:28,259
Sit still. How many times are you going back and forth?

473
00:27:28,329 --> 00:27:29,699
You think I want to go?

474
00:27:30,459 --> 00:27:32,199
- Hey, Tae Gu.
- Yes?

475
00:27:32,599 --> 00:27:34,839
Looks like we aren't the only ones here to suck up to Bbakgu tonight.

476
00:27:35,769 --> 00:27:37,499
Everyone thinks the same way.

477
00:27:37,969 --> 00:27:40,569
How do we break through that? Let's just go.

478
00:27:40,639 --> 00:27:43,239
No way, after coming all this way, we can't just leave.

479
00:27:43,439 --> 00:27:45,309
I'm definitely getting a seat over there tonight.

480
00:27:47,579 --> 00:27:48,579
Where are you going?

481
00:27:50,519 --> 00:27:52,589
- Whose drink are you having?
- What the...

482
00:27:52,689 --> 00:27:56,219
- Look who's here. Su Kyung.
- Please pour me a drink.

483
00:27:56,289 --> 00:27:57,359
Sure.

484
00:28:12,009 --> 00:28:13,009
Producer Park...

485
00:28:14,609 --> 00:28:16,139
Producer Park, I bought some ice cream.

486
00:28:16,779 --> 00:28:19,948
- What did you get?
- I got bars, popsicles, and cones.

487
00:28:19,949 --> 00:28:21,549
- Are you okay?
- Nice.

488
00:28:21,619 --> 00:28:23,049
- You okay?
- What?

489
00:28:24,989 --> 00:28:25,989
What's this?

490
00:28:26,349 --> 00:28:28,559
Kang Tae Gu, what are you doing down there?

491
00:28:30,819 --> 00:28:31,829
You scared me.

492
00:28:32,459 --> 00:28:33,459
What else?

493
00:28:33,659 --> 00:28:35,059
I came to mix you a drink, Producer Park.

494
00:28:35,659 --> 00:28:36,659
Allow me to pour you one.

495
00:28:37,499 --> 00:28:38,999
All right, pour me a glass.

496
00:28:39,669 --> 00:28:40,969
Yes, thank you.

497
00:28:45,509 --> 00:28:46,509
Okay.

498
00:28:51,679 --> 00:28:52,749
As expected.

499
00:28:53,279 --> 00:28:54,919
- Park Gu Young!
- Is a real man!

500
00:28:54,979 --> 00:28:56,619
- Park Gu Young!
- Is a real man!

501
00:28:56,679 --> 00:28:57,679
Applause.

502
00:28:57,849 --> 00:29:00,689
- Applause.
- Stop it, stop it, stop it.

503
00:29:00,749 --> 00:29:03,389
- Hey, you're pretty good at this.
- Just say the word.

504
00:29:03,459 --> 00:29:05,689
I'll mix drinks for you all night.

505
00:29:05,759 --> 00:29:08,929
Look at this brownnoser. What a total suck-up.

506
00:29:10,099 --> 00:29:11,568
By the way, Chan Sung, didn't you say...

507
00:29:11,569 --> 00:29:12,929
you had to leave early for tomorrow?

508
00:29:12,999 --> 00:29:14,939
- I did, but...
- Yes?

509
00:29:17,069 --> 00:29:18,669
I think I can stay a bit longer.

510
00:29:19,609 --> 00:29:20,939
All right, sounds good then.

511
00:29:23,639 --> 00:29:25,409
Well, the more the merrier, right?

512
00:29:25,709 --> 00:29:27,679
I really love company dinner culture.

513
00:29:27,779 --> 00:29:29,948
It's only at places like this where we can have candid...

514
00:29:29,949 --> 00:29:31,689
Hey, why are your glasses empty?

515
00:29:31,889 --> 00:29:33,119
Fill them up.

516
00:29:33,549 --> 00:29:35,719
Producer Park. Let me pour yours.

517
00:29:37,789 --> 00:29:38,959
Producer Park, so about what I was saying...

518
00:29:39,029 --> 00:29:40,989
- For our sketch this time...
- I'm out of cigarettes.

519
00:29:41,429 --> 00:29:42,429
Go buy me some cigarettes.

520
00:29:46,169 --> 00:29:48,039
- Excuse me?
- Why, you don't want to?

521
00:29:48,239 --> 00:29:49,769
Didn't you just say something about a sketch?

522
00:29:52,609 --> 00:29:53,609
Of course I want to.

523
00:29:53,739 --> 00:29:55,409
I run the 100 meters in 12 seconds, you know.

524
00:29:55,839 --> 00:29:57,709
Start counting. Here I go.

525
00:29:59,409 --> 00:30:01,579
Man, look at that guy.

526
00:30:04,379 --> 00:30:06,649
- A pack of cigarettes, please.
- Which one?

527
00:30:07,519 --> 00:30:08,858
Give me the strongest one you have. The one that will kill the fastest.

528
00:30:08,859 --> 00:30:10,389
Hurry. Here.

529
00:30:10,459 --> 00:30:13,359
- Producer Park.
- Caught you red-handed, you punk.

530
00:30:13,889 --> 00:30:16,128
- Dumping your drink, are you?
- I'm sorry, Producer Park.

531
00:30:16,129 --> 00:30:18,269
My stomach just happens to be really upset today.

532
00:30:18,329 --> 00:30:19,469
Cut the crap.

533
00:30:24,969 --> 00:30:26,739
Drink it. That's your punishment for slacking off.

534
00:30:30,679 --> 00:30:33,948
All right, Producer Park. I have a special talent.

535
00:30:33,949 --> 00:30:35,319
Allow me to show it to you.

536
00:30:44,119 --> 00:30:47,359
Is this punk kidding me? Seriously. Drink up.

537
00:30:48,329 --> 00:30:50,529
Producer Park, I'll drink it for him.

538
00:30:50,599 --> 00:30:51,599
Wussing out?

539
00:30:52,969 --> 00:30:54,939
You guys are no fun. Get lost.

540
00:30:55,199 --> 00:30:56,569
No, sir. Well then...

541
00:30:57,039 --> 00:30:59,569
I'll drink it in a fun way.

542
00:30:59,639 --> 00:31:00,909
That's right. You've got to drink it.

543
00:31:00,969 --> 00:31:01,979
- Bottoms up.
- Yes, sir.

544
00:31:02,039 --> 00:31:05,609
- Down the hatch.
- All right, clap. Applaud.

545
00:31:06,709 --> 00:31:08,479
Okay, clap, clap, clap.

546
00:31:08,549 --> 00:31:09,949
- Clap.
- Bottoms up.

547
00:31:10,019 --> 00:31:11,019
Let's go.

548
00:31:25,699 --> 00:31:28,139
What's this, all of a sudden? Have you lost your mind?

549
00:31:29,399 --> 00:31:32,169
Yes. I'm about to lose it.

550
00:31:38,979 --> 00:31:40,079
So let's stop right here.

551
00:31:45,289 --> 00:31:46,289
Let's go. Get up.

552
00:31:48,049 --> 00:31:49,059
Are you getting up or not?

553
00:31:50,259 --> 00:31:51,629
Why, you little punk.

554
00:32:01,699 --> 00:32:02,898
Just because people call you "Producer"...

555
00:32:02,899 --> 00:32:04,499
you must think you're something special.

556
00:32:04,909 --> 00:32:06,638
You do know all the comedians here...

557
00:32:06,639 --> 00:32:07,939
trash-talk you behind your back, right?

558
00:32:08,279 --> 00:32:10,309
They say your comedy sense sucks, but your character sucks even more.

559
00:32:11,879 --> 00:32:13,548
- What?
- I feel like crap tonight,

560
00:32:13,549 --> 00:32:14,709
so I'll be taking my leave.

561
00:32:17,819 --> 00:32:19,189
See you at the new sketch review.

562
00:32:25,129 --> 00:32:26,129
Let's go.

563
00:32:28,029 --> 00:32:29,029
Let's go.

564
00:32:46,679 --> 00:32:47,679
Hey, Kang Tae Gu.

565
00:32:48,179 --> 00:32:50,349
- Kang Tae Gu.
- Producer. Sir!

566
00:32:50,419 --> 00:32:51,819
Hey, who does that punk think he is?

567
00:32:51,889 --> 00:32:53,589
Sir, that's Tae Gu.

568
00:32:58,446 --> 00:33:00,616
Tae Gu, your mouth will freeze crooked.

569
00:33:05,826 --> 00:33:09,756
What have I done? What on earth did I...

570
00:33:16,796 --> 00:33:18,266
That idiot is at it again.

571
00:33:20,406 --> 00:33:21,606
Leave him alone.

572
00:33:30,616 --> 00:33:31,646
Sit down.

573
00:33:32,416 --> 00:33:33,416
Sit.

574
00:33:35,016 --> 00:33:36,616
I told you, why did you have to butt in?

575
00:33:36,686 --> 00:33:39,226
I was handling it so smoothly all on my own.

576
00:33:40,626 --> 00:33:42,426
You already look pathetic, and watching you do that...

577
00:33:42,496 --> 00:33:43,926
pissed me off even more, all right?

578
00:33:44,726 --> 00:33:48,736
Forget it. What's done is done. It's fine.

579
00:33:50,466 --> 00:33:52,606
Yes, you're right.

580
00:33:55,976 --> 00:33:58,036
That Bbak Gu Young...

581
00:34:01,306 --> 00:34:02,316
Hey.

582
00:34:02,816 --> 00:34:04,516
When I make it big, I'm getting revenge on Bbakgu.

583
00:34:04,816 --> 00:34:06,716
I'll make sure he never sets foot in this industry again.

584
00:34:06,786 --> 00:34:08,116
Well, you know what I'll do?

585
00:34:08,186 --> 00:34:10,316
I'll keep him right by my side and slowly gaslight him...

586
00:34:10,386 --> 00:34:11,386
until he withers away and dies.

587
00:34:11,456 --> 00:34:13,626
- Sounds good.
- I already took care of it.

588
00:34:19,996 --> 00:34:20,996
What's this?

589
00:34:22,296 --> 00:34:24,636
Did you seriously pack this up in all that chaos?

590
00:34:25,236 --> 00:34:26,436
It's a waste otherwise.

591
00:34:27,066 --> 00:34:28,606
Today's team dinner must have cost a fortune.

592
00:34:30,136 --> 00:34:32,176
Man. You're the scariest of all, you bastard.

593
00:34:32,246 --> 00:34:34,106
Look at you. Good job, buddy.

594
00:34:34,176 --> 00:34:35,976
- Good job, buddy.
- Shoot.

595
00:34:37,516 --> 00:34:41,286
- Look at this. Here, not this one.
- Shoot, what? What's this?

596
00:34:41,986 --> 00:34:43,886
- Yes.
- The light turned on.

597
00:35:03,736 --> 00:35:05,906
- Are you cold?
- Gosh...

598
00:35:06,806 --> 00:35:09,246
- Hold on, man.
- Hey.

599
00:35:09,316 --> 00:35:12,686
- Hold still for a second.
- Stop creeping me out, man.

600
00:35:12,746 --> 00:35:14,146
Today felt so long.

601
00:35:17,856 --> 00:35:18,856
Yes.

602
00:35:21,256 --> 00:35:22,996
It looks so close from here.

603
00:35:25,266 --> 00:35:28,026
Why is getting from here to there so hard?

604
00:35:31,396 --> 00:35:32,836
Back when we were starting out,

605
00:35:33,736 --> 00:35:37,476
we used to drink right here, staring up at that sign.

606
00:35:38,806 --> 00:35:39,946
We would write comedy sketches...

607
00:35:41,606 --> 00:35:43,746
and talk about what cars we would buy.

608
00:35:46,316 --> 00:35:49,416
We were completely broke back then. Just a bottle of soju and...

609
00:35:49,486 --> 00:35:51,186
- Hard candy.
- Hard candy.

610
00:35:54,726 --> 00:35:57,326
It feels like yesterday, but it's already been ten years.

611
00:36:15,476 --> 00:36:16,476
You're right.

612
00:36:19,886 --> 00:36:21,446
Ten years have already passed.

613
00:36:38,366 --> 00:36:40,506
Look at him slacking off since he's almost discharged.

614
00:36:40,566 --> 00:36:42,006
Hurry your butt over here.

615
00:36:43,206 --> 00:36:44,406
Loyalty.

616
00:36:45,076 --> 00:36:48,276
Sergeant Kang Tae Gu reporting for discharge.

617
00:36:48,346 --> 00:36:50,646
- At ease.
- At ease.

618
00:36:51,046 --> 00:36:52,516
- Thank you.
- All right, salute.

619
00:36:52,586 --> 00:36:53,986
Look at you slacking, you punk.

620
00:36:54,716 --> 00:36:57,286
- Says the unemployed guy. Come on.
- What...

621
00:36:57,356 --> 00:37:00,256
How many times must I say I'm studying for the exam, you jerk?

622
00:37:01,286 --> 00:37:04,896
He'll work at his dad's hospital once he finishes med school.

623
00:37:04,956 --> 00:37:05,966
And you?

624
00:37:06,126 --> 00:37:08,226
You're going to your dad's auto repair shop.

625
00:37:09,096 --> 00:37:11,336
What about me? What am I supposed to do?

626
00:37:11,736 --> 00:37:13,566
Are you really going to work at your dad's shop?

627
00:37:13,636 --> 00:37:16,536
That's why he majored in automotive maintenance.

628
00:37:16,606 --> 00:37:20,576
- Forget about that. Worry about me.
- Just go study.

629
00:37:20,646 --> 00:37:22,816
- Studying isn't my thing.
- I'm not working at the shop.

630
00:37:24,616 --> 00:37:25,616
Man.

631
00:37:25,686 --> 00:37:27,886
Spoiled talk like that ruins my buzz.

632
00:37:34,286 --> 00:37:35,596
I want to try comedy.

633
00:37:37,056 --> 00:37:38,126
For real.

634
00:37:39,366 --> 00:37:40,496
Seriously.

635
00:37:43,666 --> 00:37:44,896
What? You want to do what?

636
00:37:47,406 --> 00:37:48,636
Do you guys remember?

637
00:37:50,976 --> 00:37:52,406
Back at our broadcasting festival.

638
00:38:12,996 --> 00:38:13,996
That day,

639
00:38:15,496 --> 00:38:17,466
I can never forget that feeling.

640
00:38:25,576 --> 00:38:26,846
I have to do this.

641
00:38:28,146 --> 00:38:29,216
I want to bet my life...

642
00:38:30,376 --> 00:38:31,616
on comedy.

643
00:38:34,986 --> 00:38:36,916
Right.

644
00:38:37,716 --> 00:38:39,256
Hey, come on.

645
00:38:39,956 --> 00:38:41,856
You think you can make a living doing that?

646
00:38:41,926 --> 00:38:44,326
There are plenty of funny people out there.

647
00:38:44,396 --> 00:38:45,396
Just ten years.

648
00:38:46,396 --> 00:38:48,026
I'll give it my all for ten years,

649
00:38:48,736 --> 00:38:50,236
and if it doesn't work out, I'll quit clean.

650
00:38:52,036 --> 00:38:53,166
So...

651
00:39:07,086 --> 00:39:08,086
what do you say?

652
00:39:10,916 --> 00:39:12,126
Do you want to do it with me?

653
00:39:20,566 --> 00:39:21,726
Just for ten years.

654
00:39:23,466 --> 00:39:24,736
Just ten years.

655
00:39:26,436 --> 00:39:27,506
Let's do it together.

656
00:39:57,766 --> 00:40:01,936
To all the valued customers visiting our department store today,

657
00:40:02,006 --> 00:40:04,436
we regret to inform you...

658
00:40:04,606 --> 00:40:08,506
that the second basement level parking is currently full...

659
00:40:08,576 --> 00:40:09,846
Whoever is late today owes 1,000 dollars.

660
00:40:10,546 --> 00:40:11,546
Okay...

661
00:40:11,616 --> 00:40:15,286
Welcome, we love having you here. Yes, welcome.

662
00:40:15,456 --> 00:40:16,456
Yes.

663
00:40:20,256 --> 00:40:21,286
All right.

664
00:40:21,856 --> 00:40:25,396
My fellow Balbalta members, I think the time has come.

665
00:40:26,896 --> 00:40:29,836
Shall we head over together? Poof.

666
00:40:31,636 --> 00:40:33,606
(I'm Heading Out Now Too)

667
00:40:33,966 --> 00:40:34,966
Hey.

668
00:40:35,536 --> 00:40:37,006
- Where are you going again?
- Darn it, you scared me.

669
00:40:37,076 --> 00:40:38,536
It's not even time to switch shifts yet.

670
00:40:38,606 --> 00:40:40,976
If the manager comes, tell him I went to the restroom.

671
00:40:41,646 --> 00:40:43,176
Where are you going?

672
00:40:43,876 --> 00:40:44,976
To my real job.

673
00:40:46,246 --> 00:40:48,446
Order me some hangover soup, will you?

674
00:40:48,816 --> 00:40:49,986
Stop drinking so much.

675
00:40:50,486 --> 00:40:51,486
Every single night,

676
00:40:51,556 --> 00:40:53,186
you drink and fool around with customers,

677
00:40:53,526 --> 00:40:55,596
and during the day, you just lie here like a corpse.

678
00:40:55,996 --> 00:40:58,656
My stomach. Help me.

679
00:40:59,766 --> 00:41:01,996
- What now? Does it hurt again?
- My stomach...

680
00:41:02,796 --> 00:41:05,565
That's how you earn money and make a living.

681
00:41:05,566 --> 00:41:06,636
That really hurts.

682
00:41:07,206 --> 00:41:10,736
- I'm leaving now too.
- It hurts. It really hurts.

683
00:41:10,806 --> 00:41:13,006
- Mr. Jung, I'm off.
- Hey, tell...

684
00:41:13,446 --> 00:41:15,006
Tae Gu and Nam Il to come this weekend.

685
00:41:15,076 --> 00:41:16,416
We need to put up shelves in the storage room.

686
00:41:16,876 --> 00:41:18,945
- Okay.
- Work it off with manual labour.

687
00:41:18,946 --> 00:41:20,886
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

688
00:41:24,716 --> 00:41:26,656
Pepperoni with extra cheese, right?

689
00:41:31,896 --> 00:41:32,896
(Tasty Pizza)

690
00:41:34,826 --> 00:41:35,836
(Asura)

691
00:41:35,896 --> 00:41:37,136
(Kim Nam Il: Leaving Too. Got 1,000 Dollars?)

692
00:41:37,196 --> 00:41:39,606
(Leaving Now)

693
00:42:49,036 --> 00:42:50,406
(2017 QBN Open Auditions For New Comedic Actors)

694
00:42:50,476 --> 00:42:51,806
(Kang Tae Gu, Kim Nam Il, Han Jun Seo)

695
00:43:11,593 --> 00:43:13,723
The more I think about it, the madder I get.

696
00:43:14,263 --> 00:43:15,633
Can he do whatever he wants as a producer?

697
00:43:15,863 --> 00:43:18,033
Who pulls an old-school power trip like that nowadays?

698
00:43:18,733 --> 00:43:21,503
That producer is infamous for having a terrible personality.

699
00:43:21,563 --> 00:43:23,573
- Unbelievable.
- He keeps telling me...

700
00:43:23,903 --> 00:43:26,473
- that I look unlikeable.
- That crazy bastard!

701
00:43:29,813 --> 00:43:31,843
Babe, what if people from your company see you?

702
00:43:31,913 --> 00:43:34,083
Is he blind? I mean,

703
00:43:34,913 --> 00:43:37,013
where else in the world could you find...

704
00:43:37,553 --> 00:43:38,623
someone this adorably unlikeable?

705
00:43:39,423 --> 00:43:41,423
That's only true for you.

706
00:43:43,853 --> 00:43:46,293
- Just sit down and eat.
- Na Yeon.

707
00:43:47,963 --> 00:43:48,963
Hey.

708
00:43:51,163 --> 00:43:53,263
Say hello. This is Jung Tae Hoon. We joined the company together.

709
00:43:54,863 --> 00:43:55,873
Hello.

710
00:43:57,133 --> 00:43:58,643
I'm Kim Nam Il.

711
00:43:58,943 --> 00:43:59,943
Hello.

712
00:44:00,243 --> 00:44:01,543
This is my boyfriend, Kim Nam Il.

713
00:44:04,043 --> 00:44:05,043
Na Yeon.

714
00:44:05,113 --> 00:44:06,843
That ESG portfolio I asked for earlier,

715
00:44:06,913 --> 00:44:08,313
could you send it over by today?

716
00:44:08,513 --> 00:44:10,053
Sure, I'll bring it over as soon as I can.

717
00:44:10,253 --> 00:44:13,752
How could I dare make a senior associate run back and forth?

718
00:44:13,753 --> 00:44:16,093
I'll come over to your desk.

719
00:44:16,923 --> 00:44:18,393
Senior associate?

720
00:44:19,363 --> 00:44:22,033
You didn't know? Na Yeon was promoted last month.

721
00:44:23,033 --> 00:44:24,233
Well, you see...

722
00:44:27,863 --> 00:44:30,473
Hey, your team is calling you. Go on, hurry.

723
00:44:32,373 --> 00:44:33,373
See you later.

724
00:44:33,443 --> 00:44:36,343
- Nice meeting you.
- Yes, enjoy your lunch.

725
00:44:38,983 --> 00:44:41,313
Seriously, he talks way too much.

726
00:44:41,813 --> 00:44:43,853
The food got cold because of him. Let's eat quickly.

727
00:44:50,053 --> 00:44:51,323
Why didn't you tell me?

728
00:44:54,323 --> 00:44:58,393
I just forgot. It's not that big of a deal anyway.

729
00:45:04,703 --> 00:45:06,273
Yes, I guess so.

730
00:45:07,503 --> 00:45:09,413
Let's eat before lunch break ends.

731
00:45:09,873 --> 00:45:10,873
Okay.

732
00:45:15,383 --> 00:45:18,653
He kept insisting on buying me a new car.

733
00:45:19,083 --> 00:45:22,153
Ever since he switched to that big corporation,

734
00:45:22,223 --> 00:45:23,523
he's gotten way too big for his britches.

735
00:45:23,923 --> 00:45:25,593
Come to think of it,

736
00:45:25,663 --> 00:45:28,323
my son and your second one are the same age, right?

737
00:45:28,693 --> 00:45:31,663
Is he still running around trying to be a comedian or whatever?

738
00:45:31,793 --> 00:45:33,103
He wasn't funny at all.

739
00:45:33,233 --> 00:45:35,702
If he were young, I'd understand.

740
00:45:35,703 --> 00:45:37,572
With his ageing father and sick brother like this,

741
00:45:37,573 --> 00:45:40,443
he should pull himself together and act like a responsible adult.

742
00:45:40,503 --> 00:45:42,913
- Hello, sir. You're here?
- Hey.

743
00:45:43,343 --> 00:45:44,913
Man, it's so hot.

744
00:45:45,583 --> 00:45:46,783
Why is it so hot today?

745
00:45:48,343 --> 00:45:50,853
- Didn't see you there, sir.
- Hi, Tae Gu.

746
00:45:51,453 --> 00:45:53,353
Anyway, I'll wait at home.

747
00:45:53,423 --> 00:45:55,993
- Call me when you're done.
- Sure, see you later.

748
00:45:57,623 --> 00:45:59,023
(Eunhye Auto Repair Shop)

749
00:45:59,593 --> 00:46:01,723
He complained about his knees, but he looks fine.

750
00:46:02,023 --> 00:46:03,293
What brings you here without calling?

751
00:46:04,163 --> 00:46:07,503
I came for warranty service. The back door is acting up again.

752
00:46:08,003 --> 00:46:10,973
- How on earth did you fix it?
- Warranty service, my foot.

753
00:46:11,033 --> 00:46:12,143
You don't even pay for repairs.

754
00:46:13,643 --> 00:46:16,013
Dad, what are we going to do with this shameless punk?

755
00:46:19,543 --> 00:46:20,713
It's so hot.

756
00:46:22,853 --> 00:46:23,953
Get me something to drink.

757
00:46:24,513 --> 00:46:26,823
- Make it cold, with ice.
- Why, you little...

758
00:46:27,253 --> 00:46:28,853
If you order your disabled brother around,

759
00:46:28,923 --> 00:46:30,223
he'll just end up doing it.

760
00:46:31,293 --> 00:46:32,563
I'll be back in a flash.

761
00:46:46,373 --> 00:46:47,843
It's so hot out in the scorching sun.

762
00:46:48,673 --> 00:46:51,213
I told you to put up a tarp here. It doesn't even cost that much.

763
00:46:54,883 --> 00:46:55,953
Need any help?

764
00:47:01,623 --> 00:47:04,593
You're trying so hard to pretend you don't hear me.

765
00:47:05,253 --> 00:47:06,263
Right?

766
00:47:22,273 --> 00:47:24,013
So, do you have some free time today?

767
00:47:24,143 --> 00:47:25,543
No, I have to go.

768
00:47:26,313 --> 00:47:27,413
I have some things to clean up.

769
00:47:28,883 --> 00:47:31,653
Dad, can you look at Tae Gu's car first?

770
00:47:32,823 --> 00:47:33,823
Please?

771
00:47:35,183 --> 00:47:36,523
He says he's busy today.

772
00:47:36,593 --> 00:47:37,953
Don't you see all the cars parked over there?

773
00:47:39,763 --> 00:47:41,863
But still...

774
00:47:42,193 --> 00:47:43,193
Forget it.

775
00:47:43,893 --> 00:47:44,933
I'll come back next time.

776
00:47:45,493 --> 00:47:46,933
Hey, Tae Gu, at least eat before you go.

777
00:47:48,103 --> 00:47:49,103
No, it's okay.

778
00:47:50,303 --> 00:47:51,333
Even if I can't be a good son,

779
00:47:52,033 --> 00:47:53,803
I should at least let Dad eat in peace.

780
00:47:55,573 --> 00:47:58,313
Dad, I'm leaving,

781
00:47:58,573 --> 00:47:59,643
so please wipe that scowl off your face.

782
00:48:00,283 --> 00:48:01,343
You'll scare the customers.

783
00:48:02,953 --> 00:48:03,953
See you, Hyun Gu.

784
00:48:06,153 --> 00:48:07,753
Come on, I told you to eat first.

785
00:48:09,523 --> 00:48:10,523
Hey!

786
00:48:14,663 --> 00:48:15,663
Seriously.

787
00:48:21,763 --> 00:48:24,103
Call Kang Tae Gu and tell him, as long as I'm here,

788
00:48:24,173 --> 00:48:26,103
don't even dream of coming to pitch a new sketch.

789
00:48:26,703 --> 00:48:30,373
He's banned from the station entirely. Got it?

790
00:48:30,443 --> 00:48:31,443
Yes, understood.

791
00:48:31,773 --> 00:48:34,013
That arrogant punk.

792
00:48:35,513 --> 00:48:36,753
How dare he mess with a producer?

793
00:48:37,013 --> 00:48:39,583
Full of fight as always, Senior Park.

794
00:48:40,523 --> 00:48:41,523
What are you doing here?

795
00:48:41,853 --> 00:48:43,753
What are you doing here? Aren't you in New York until year-end?

796
00:48:43,823 --> 00:48:46,763
Yes, I was. The director summoned me urgently.

797
00:48:47,463 --> 00:48:50,993
He's been looking for you too for a while.

798
00:48:51,333 --> 00:48:53,633
- Me? Looking for me?
- Yes.

799
00:48:54,633 --> 00:48:56,903
Standards and Practices Department out of the blue?

800
00:48:57,233 --> 00:48:59,743
- That's a demotion.
- Yes, it's a demotion.

801
00:49:01,573 --> 00:49:03,813
I heard you were entertained by CEO Oh again, right?

802
00:49:04,013 --> 00:49:05,813
I told you to keep your greed in check.

803
00:49:06,013 --> 00:49:08,083
- You really are unbelievable.
- Entertained...

804
00:49:08,283 --> 00:49:10,883
Entertained? It was just networking.

805
00:49:11,113 --> 00:49:13,283
Can't a producer be friends with an agency CEO?

806
00:49:13,353 --> 00:49:15,023
Friends?

807
00:49:15,223 --> 00:49:16,793
So were you also close friends with the agency's rookies...

808
00:49:16,853 --> 00:49:18,453
when you were out drinking with them?

809
00:49:18,523 --> 00:49:20,623
- But...
- You sure have a lot of friends.

810
00:49:22,023 --> 00:49:24,393
Just shut your mouth and pack your bags.

811
00:49:24,663 --> 00:49:25,703
Senior, please.

812
00:49:25,763 --> 00:49:27,663
You have to at least pretend to reflect on your actions...

813
00:49:27,703 --> 00:49:29,333
so that I can bring you back later.

814
00:49:29,873 --> 00:49:31,003
Just go for now.

815
00:49:31,733 --> 00:49:33,503
Then who's replacing me?

816
00:49:34,673 --> 00:49:36,373
So, while this is quite sudden,

817
00:49:36,673 --> 00:49:38,443
I've been assigned to replace Senior Park.

818
00:49:39,683 --> 00:49:40,713
I'll be blunt.

819
00:49:40,913 --> 00:49:43,283
Word of Senior Park getting fired has leaked to the press.

820
00:49:43,353 --> 00:49:44,713
People are talking all over the place.

821
00:49:45,113 --> 00:49:46,983
We need a new sketch to divert their attention.

822
00:49:50,653 --> 00:49:52,023
Put something together and bring it to me.

823
00:49:58,393 --> 00:49:59,433
Well...

824
00:50:00,463 --> 00:50:02,003
Us?

825
00:50:02,833 --> 00:50:04,472
- We'll do our best.
- We'll do our best.

826
00:50:04,473 --> 00:50:05,842
- We'll give it our all.
- We'll work hard.

827
00:50:05,843 --> 00:50:06,872
We'll do a great job.

828
00:50:06,873 --> 00:50:08,343
- We'll do our best.
- We'll make it great.

829
00:50:08,403 --> 00:50:10,043
- We'll do our best.
- We won't let you down.

830
00:50:21,923 --> 00:50:22,923
Hello.

831
00:50:24,423 --> 00:50:25,523
Let's get to it.

832
00:50:26,093 --> 00:50:28,323
Right now, every sketch takes too long to get to the punchline.

833
00:50:28,863 --> 00:50:30,333
So we should just do a bridge segment.

834
00:50:30,433 --> 00:50:34,003
Set it up openly like a talent show, and jump in between the sketches...

835
00:50:34,063 --> 00:50:36,273
to smash gourds and break wooden boards.

836
00:50:38,503 --> 00:50:39,543
Darn it.

837
00:50:40,343 --> 00:50:42,003
Feats of strength are so old school.

838
00:50:42,913 --> 00:50:46,013
Hey, why don't we go for something a little more primal?

839
00:50:46,883 --> 00:50:49,153
- Animal impressions.
- That's been done to death.

840
00:51:02,393 --> 00:51:04,333
You psycho. You're embarrassing us. Stop.

841
00:51:05,063 --> 00:51:07,733
You freak, cut it out. Stop it.

842
00:51:31,723 --> 00:51:32,723
An elephant.

843
00:51:44,073 --> 00:51:46,002
- I think you're missing the point.
- Sorry about this.

844
00:51:46,003 --> 00:51:47,943
- No, really.
- These are the eyes, the trunk...

845
00:51:48,003 --> 00:51:49,003
See, it's an elephant.

846
00:51:49,073 --> 00:51:50,913
- No.
- Where's she going?

847
00:51:51,043 --> 00:51:52,172
Just stop explaining it.

848
00:51:52,173 --> 00:51:54,313
She might laugh tomorrow, you know.

849
00:51:54,383 --> 00:51:55,582
How are you ever going to go back there...

850
00:51:55,583 --> 00:51:56,853
after humiliating yourself like that?

851
00:51:57,013 --> 00:51:59,013
Hey, that girl is the weird one.

852
00:51:59,583 --> 00:52:02,183
Whatever, forget it. Anyway, how should we end it?

853
00:52:02,523 --> 00:52:04,723
- He's just embarrassed.
- Seriously.

854
00:52:06,523 --> 00:52:08,193
Or maybe instead, hey.

855
00:52:08,563 --> 00:52:10,263
Let's go visual, rely completely on visuals.

856
00:52:10,433 --> 00:52:11,933
Barefoot, let's go barefoot,

857
00:52:11,993 --> 00:52:13,233
totally lean into a wild-man concept,

858
00:52:13,533 --> 00:52:15,503
and put a pigeon on your shoulder.

859
00:52:16,033 --> 00:52:17,033
That's weak.

860
00:52:17,303 --> 00:52:19,543
- What else should we do, then?
- Too weak. It's weak.

861
00:52:19,603 --> 00:52:21,203
Then put a real pigeon on him.

862
00:52:21,673 --> 00:52:23,843
Sounds great. That'll pass instantly.

863
00:52:23,913 --> 00:52:25,573
- Right. Put one on.
- Okay, let's go with that.

864
00:52:25,643 --> 00:52:26,643
- Do it.
- I like it.

865
00:52:26,713 --> 00:52:28,713
Go catch a pigeon. Go!

866
00:53:02,313 --> 00:53:03,513
How many times do I have to tell you?

867
00:53:03,583 --> 00:53:05,553
I'm staying in Seoul for good now.

868
00:53:06,123 --> 00:53:08,453
Should we all get together soon? Let's gather everyone up.

869
00:53:08,553 --> 00:53:10,493
Hold on, I've got another call. Don't hang up.

870
00:53:12,123 --> 00:53:13,163
Hey, Young Ju.

871
00:53:14,563 --> 00:53:15,793
Word got out already?

872
00:53:16,363 --> 00:53:19,403
Yes, I finally moved out.

873
00:53:20,163 --> 00:53:22,263
No, not by myself. I'm staying with my sister.

874
00:53:22,533 --> 00:53:23,533
Yes.

875
00:53:23,603 --> 00:53:25,533
Hey, I think my cab is here. I'll call you later.

876
00:53:25,603 --> 00:53:26,603
Taxi!

877
00:53:33,143 --> 00:53:34,143
What the...

878
00:53:39,053 --> 00:53:40,083
Guys, what's this?

879
00:53:40,683 --> 00:53:41,683
What?

880
00:53:42,223 --> 00:53:44,493
- What's this?
- What?

881
00:53:46,193 --> 00:53:47,223
What's that?

882
00:53:51,663 --> 00:53:53,503
What do we do?

883
00:53:54,203 --> 00:53:56,472
What do we do? Hey, it's moving.

884
00:53:56,473 --> 00:53:58,273
Get back. It's coming out.

885
00:53:58,333 --> 00:54:00,073
- Darn it...
- Hey, this... Hey.

886
00:54:00,143 --> 00:54:01,143
Hey, where are you going?

887
00:54:01,843 --> 00:54:02,843
Shoot.

888
00:54:06,213 --> 00:54:08,043
Hey, it just made eye contact with me.

889
00:54:09,613 --> 00:54:10,713
Hey.

890
00:54:15,853 --> 00:54:17,053
Call an ambulance!

891
00:54:17,623 --> 00:54:18,653
Stay back.

892
00:54:22,733 --> 00:54:25,433
(Soojung Villa, Dream Villa)

893
00:54:28,433 --> 00:54:29,433
Excuse me.

894
00:54:33,503 --> 00:54:34,543
What are you doing?

895
00:54:35,643 --> 00:54:36,673
Who are you?

896
00:54:46,883 --> 00:54:47,923
Hey, you in the black hoodie!

897
00:55:14,183 --> 00:55:16,083
Comedy has two basic rules.

898
00:55:16,913 --> 00:55:19,253
Repetition and a twist.

899
00:55:25,993 --> 00:55:26,993
Hey.

900
00:55:30,263 --> 00:55:31,963
Life follows the exact same rules.

901
00:55:34,133 --> 00:55:35,633
Hey. Who are you?

902
00:55:37,703 --> 00:55:38,903
Hey, who are you?

903
00:55:39,603 --> 00:55:40,673
Why is she so fast?

904
00:55:42,103 --> 00:55:43,113
Hey!

905
00:55:46,713 --> 00:55:47,713
Oh, no.

906
00:55:50,353 --> 00:55:51,353
(Asura)

907
00:55:51,413 --> 00:55:53,453
When the days that felt exciting just to dream...

908
00:55:54,853 --> 00:55:57,153
start to feel like a miserable loop,

909
00:56:08,763 --> 00:56:10,073
what we need right now...

910
00:56:19,513 --> 00:56:20,683
is just one plot twist.

911
00:57:38,323 --> 00:57:39,993
I'm so sorry.

912
00:57:43,663 --> 00:57:45,663
Goodness.

913
00:57:45,993 --> 00:57:50,403
- You scared me.
- Do you have any drinks...

914
00:57:50,903 --> 00:57:52,203
that give you energy?

915
00:57:52,703 --> 00:57:56,942
- Give me three, please.
- Three. Yes, here.

916
00:57:56,943 --> 00:57:58,413
Be careful, they're glass.

917
00:58:03,213 --> 00:58:04,253
Oh, what do I do?

918
00:58:05,283 --> 00:58:08,183
I gave her the ones I set aside because they expired.

919
00:58:17,093 --> 00:58:20,963
(Happy Anding)

920
00:58:24,873 --> 00:58:25,873
I passed.

921
00:58:26,603 --> 00:58:29,943
I passed. I really got in. I got in.

922
00:58:41,023 --> 00:58:42,053
I got accepted.

923
00:58:42,583 --> 00:58:44,053
I got the internship.

924
00:58:45,123 --> 00:58:46,863
Look. I got in, right?

925
00:58:47,123 --> 00:58:48,293
Yes.

926
00:58:49,993 --> 00:58:52,633
This was the company I really wanted to work for.

927
00:58:53,503 --> 00:58:55,333
Today is the happiest day...

928
00:58:55,863 --> 00:58:57,103
of my whole life.

929
00:59:03,173 --> 00:59:04,873
Mine too.

930
00:59:06,643 --> 00:59:08,143
Congratulations on getting the job.

931
00:59:10,853 --> 00:59:13,653
Wait. I need to call Mom.

932
00:59:16,253 --> 00:59:18,593
Mom, I got accepted.

933
00:59:19,963 --> 00:59:22,323
Where is Dad? Put him on too.

934
00:59:23,933 --> 00:59:25,693
- I just got the text.
- Hey, you forgot this. Hey!

935
00:59:26,933 --> 00:59:28,663
- Take this.
- Hold on.

936
00:59:30,473 --> 00:59:31,473
Thank you.

937
00:59:32,233 --> 00:59:33,343
Mom.

938
01:00:05,933 --> 01:00:07,373
Just be upfront about it.

939
01:00:07,443 --> 01:00:09,843
Tell them you're their fan and like them.

940
01:00:10,013 --> 01:00:11,643
I need to at least see her face to report her.

941
01:00:11,713 --> 01:00:12,913
Why report her?

942
01:00:13,143 --> 01:00:14,743
So I can beat the crap out of her myself.

943
01:00:15,743 --> 01:00:18,753
Hello. You're Asura, right?

944
01:00:18,853 --> 01:00:21,023
I know I've seen her somewhere...

945
01:00:21,083 --> 01:00:23,553
A crazy girl lives in this neighbourhood.

946
01:00:25,593 --> 01:00:26,793
How dare you?

947
01:00:27,323 --> 01:00:28,823
I gave that pathetic nobody a shot out of pity.

948
01:00:29,323 --> 01:00:30,593
When it's not working, it's not working.

949
01:00:30,663 --> 01:00:32,162
If we were to just quit right now,

950
01:00:32,163 --> 01:00:35,163
do you think there's anyone who would truly try to stop us?

951
01:00:35,763 --> 01:00:36,773
Nobody.

952
01:00:37,233 --> 01:00:38,703
No. If I were going to end it like this,

953
01:00:38,728 --> 01:00:39,928
I wouldn't have started.

954
01:00:40,043 --> 01:00:42,573
Here's an ambitious new segment.

955
01:00:42,803 --> 01:00:44,343
Let's go, Asura.

956
01:00:44,673 --> 01:00:45,743
- Let's go!
- Let's go!
